  "id": "thecherrypit",
  "neon": "#ff2a5a",
  "note": "THE CHERRY PIT, on the corner of Cinder Lane and Filament Street. The room description is the brief: a windowless block of breeze-block painted arterial red, a padded vinyl door, and a pink neon cherry over it that has lost its stem and half its lower curve. So the building is a plain one-storey hall with a stage block behind it, and every bit of noise is on one false front bolted across the street face: the cherry and the name at the top, LIVE GIRLS to the left of the door, XXX over it, and a queue rail on the pavement. All three signs are neonArt with flashers (client/shared/neon-signs.js); the cherry's stem and lower curve are dead glass, and the stem catches for a blink once a cycle.\n\nIt replaced a violet cross-plan with a chrome drum, which read as a casino and was the loudest thing on a street of brick terraces even by day. The walls here are dull on purpose: by day it is a red box you would walk past, and at night the front is the only thing on the corner.\n\n⚠ NO WINDOWS, AND THE KIT IS TOLD SO. `KIT_DECLINE.strip` shuts the kit's `wall` section (it glazed the hall) and its `signRoof` (a NIGHTCLUB hoarding on legs, repeating the cherry in a stranger's hand). `ty_cherry` is in BRICK_WALL for the same reason: FACADE_MAT would paint a window grid on it.\n\n⚠ THE FALSE FRONT IS ITS OWN BOX, proud of the hall by 0.03, so every sign on it sits on a wall that exists at that plane. A sign authored on the hall's face at 0.40 would be inside it.",
  "pal": "ty_cherry",
  "replaces": "strip",
